 The OMP integration reports `omp` as the agent label, lifecycle state, and native session identity through Herdr's socket API. It does not require native process detection for the `omp` executable, and Herdr can resume an OMP pane with `omp --resume=<session>` after a server restart.
 
+## OmO / Senpi (local CLI only)
+
+```bash
+herdr integration install omo
+herdr integration install senpi
+herdr integration status
+herdr integration uninstall omo
+herdr integration uninstall senpi
+```
+
+These commands install the same Herdr-owned Senpi extension (version `1`) as
+`extensions/herdr-senpi-agent-state.ts`. Native OmO defaults to
+`~/.omo/agent`; standalone Senpi defaults to `~/.senpi/agent`. The agent directory
+must already exist; Herdr creates only the missing extensions directory.
+
+Path resolution follows the selected launcher:
+
+- OmO reads `OMO_CODING_AGENT_DIR`, then `SENPI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`, then
+  `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`. It trims whitespace and uses the first nonempty value,
+  otherwise `~/.omo/agent`. It does not search project directories or expand a
+  literal tilde in an override. Relative overrides resolve from the current directory.
+- Standalone Senpi reads `SENPI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`, then `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`.
+  The first defined value wins, including an empty value. Empty or absent values
+  select project/default lookup; `~` and `~/` in nonempty overrides expand to home.
+- Senpi project lookup selects the nearest real `.senpi/agent` directory, up to
+  100 parents, excluding symlinks and stopping before home. It then falls back to
+  `~/.senpi/agent`. Use native filesystem paths for either launcher.
+
+Run install, status, and uninstall from the same project and with the same
+variables used to launch the agent. A directory shared with Pi/OMP is refused;
+configure a separate `OMO_CODING_AGENT_DIR` or `SENPI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` instead.
+Herdr does not replace or remove unrelated files at the install filename, and
+uninstall leaves other extensions and settings untouched. Restart the agent after
+installation. `status --outdated-only` also reports local OmO/Senpi updates.
+
+This packaging is **local CLI only**. The server/API integration list, API
+install/uninstall targets, startup recommendations, and schema-derived shell
+completion targets remain unchanged until a separately versioned API is available.
+No protocol generation or API target enum is extended by these commands.
+
+The extension reports `working` while Senpi codemode has detached eval cells,
+then releases that report when the last cell settles or the session changes.
+It requires Senpi's `wake_source_state` event with source `senpi-codemode`.
+Other activity and permission prompts remain screen-detected. This integration
+does not report native session identity or enable automatic session resume.
+
